
## A
CHECK A1.create-READY-derived PASS task create --status READY with an absent mandatory input is not stored READY -- {"reasons": ["mandatory inputs unsatisfied: REQ-0901 (requirement: ABSENT)"], "task_status": "BLOCKED"}
CHECK A2.status-READY-refused PASS task status READY is refused while a mandatory input is absent -- TASK_NOT_READY
CHECK A3.claim-refused PASS claim is refused while a mandatory input is absent -- TASK_NOT_RUNNABLE
CHECK A4.replan-no-promotion PASS replan does not promote a task whose mandatory input is absent (W3-r1-replan) -- []
CHECK A5.input-provided-claimable PASS (control) once the input exists the same task is claimable -- null
CHECK A6.explicit-hold PASS a task held BLOCKED by `task status` is not runnable and `continue` does not offer it (X2-I4) -- {"continue": null, "runnable": ["TASK-0001"]}
CHECK A7.done-only-by-close PASS task status DONE is refused (DONE only through an evidence-gated close) -- TASK_STATUS_REQUIRES_OPERATION
CHECK A8.missing-dependency-no-bypass PASS a missing task dependency cannot be bypassed by `task status READY` + claim (W3-r1 bypass) -- {"claim": "TASK_NOT_RUNNABLE", "status": "TASK_NOT_READY"}

## B
CHECK B1.pending-not-claimable PASS (control) a task behind a pending gate waits and is not claimable -- [{"task": "TASK-0001", "gate": "HDG-0001", "gates": ["HDG-0001"], "reasons": ["waiting on human gate HDG-0001"]}]
CHECK B2.declined-blocks PASS a task whose gate was answered with a non-authorising option is not runnable (L3.b4.t2) -- [{"task": "TASK-0001", "reasons": ["human gate HDG-0001 was answered 'B', which does not authorise this work"]}]
CHECK B3.revoked-blocks PASS an authorising answer releases the task; revoking it blocks the task again (L3.b4.t3) -- [{"task": "TASK-0002", "reasons": ["human gate HDG-0002 was withdrawn/revoked: its authorisation no longer exists"]}]
CHECK B4.missing-gate-blocks PASS a task referencing a gate that does not exist is not runnable (L3.b4.t5) -- [{"task": "TASK-0003", "reasons": ["human gate HDG-9999 does not exist: a reference to a missing gate blocks"]}]
CHECK B5.field-removal-does-not-release PASS removing `human_gate` from the task record does not release it: the OS-written gate names the task -- [{"task": "TASK-0004", "gate": "HDG-0003", "gates": ["HDG-0003"], "reasons": ["waiting on human gate HDG-0003"]}]
CHECK B6.close-refused-while-gated PASS a task whose blocking gate is pending cannot be closed, not even with --force (L3s.1) -- {"close": "GATE_NOT_AUTHORISED", "force": "GATE_NOT_AUTHORISED"}
CHECK B7.authorised-closes PASS (control) after an authorising answer the close proceeds -- null

## C
CHECK C2.declared-forgery-refused PASS (control) declaring the forged records does not make them the worker's to write -- MUTATION_SCOPE_VIOLATION
CHECK C1.forged-t2-refused PASS a worker's hand-written gate answer and gate-derived decision inside its task are observed and refused at close (X2-E1xG2, L3.b5.9) -- {"code": "MUTATION_SCOPE_VIOLATION", "t2": [{"path": "spec/decisions/D-0901.yaml", "reason": "spec/decisions/D-0901.yaml is a decision derived from a Human Decision Gate answer: only a gov operation writes it and every such write is sealed (T2), but this one carries no seal"}, {"path": "spec/decisions/HDG-0001.yaml", "reason": "spec/decisions/HDG-0001.yaml: OS-written state (T2) changed outside a gov operation (binding BROKEN: the record was modified after the OS operation 'gate create' sealed it at 2026-09-19T05:20:42Z)"}]}
CHECK C3.os-writes-not-attributed PASS (control) the OS's own sealed gate written inside the window is not attributed to the worker -- null
CHECK C4.forged-report-refused PASS a hand-written close report is observed and refused -- MUTATION_SCOPE_VIOLATION
CHECK C5.baseline-tamper-refused PASS a rewritten claim baseline (hiding a change) is refused -- CLAIM_BASELINE_UNBOUND

## D
CHECK D1.bare-report-refused PASS a bare report (no packet, no consumed inputs, no deviations/unknowns) is refused (W5-c1/r6) -- RECEIPT_INVALID
CHECK D2.fabricated-trace-refused PASS a receipt naming a requirement that does not exist is refused (W5-r3r4) -- RECEIPT_INVALID
CHECK D3.worker-return-is-the-receipt PASS a worker return in the worker-return shape (status: success) carrying the receipt closes the task (X2-N4xW5) -- {"error_count": 0, "errors": [], "manifest_hash": "a61f01813949d7ea872056d9169d1dc89845ced19b642eb3aff97c7c6e1a66cf", "ok": true, "packet_hash": "72550109a90b46e78a38d2a661b01a744cd13ece5bb0cebecf6d763fb1baaa30", "traceability_required": true, "warning_count": 0}
CHECK D4.receipt-persisted PASS the receipt is persisted on the sealed report and the task records what it produced (task -> output edge) -- {"outputs_produced": ["tests/supp_d3.rs"], "report_keys": ["acceptance_evidence", "close_gate", "constraints_applied", "context_packet_hash", "created", "decisions_applied", "deviations", "discoveries", "evidence", "features_implemented", "files_changed", "id", "inputs_consumed", "lessons", "mutation_evidence", "observed_files_changed", "os_binding", "outcome", "outputs_produced", "proposed_decisions", "receipt_validation", "recommended_next_action", "requirements_implemented", "risks", "role", "scenarios_implemented", "session", "state_class", "status", "task", "tests", "title", "type", "unresolved", "work_completed"]}

## E
CHECK E1.self-declared-independence-rejected PASS an acceptance obligation that only declares itself independent does not satisfy TEST_POLICY independence (E1.b4.b) -- [{"task": "TASK-0001", "reasons": ["TST-0200 (acceptance) must be authored independently of the implementer (TEST_POLICY.independent_test_author_required_for), and its independence is not established from recorded authorship: no sealed close report produced its current content. `independent_of_implementer` / `author_role` are the artefact's own claims, not evidence; produce it through a test-design task closed by an independent role and session"]}]
CHECK E2.recorded-authorship-satisfies PASS (control) an obligation produced by a test-design task closed by an independent role and session satisfies it -- []
CHECK E3.author-session-cannot-implement PASS the session that authored the independent tests cannot claim the implementation, whatever role it declares -- INDEPENDENCE_VIOLATION
CHECK E4.implementer-test-data-blocks PASS test data authored by the implementer's role blocks the implementation (H4.b2) -- [{"task": "TASK-0001", "reasons": ["TST-0200 (acceptance) must be authored independently of the implementer (TEST_POLICY.independent_test_author_required_for), and its independence is not established from recorded authorship: no sealed close report produced its current content. `independent_of_implementer` / `author_role` are the artefact's own claims, not evidence; produce it through a test-design task closed by an independent role and session", "test data TD-0200 (used by TST-0200) declares itself authored by the implementer (author_role 'backend-engineer'): test-data authorship must be independent of the implementation (Contract v3 H4)"]}]
CHECK E5.planner-designates-independent-roles PASS the readiness planner's independent-test and test-data gap tasks designate independent roles -- {"independent_acceptance_tests": "independent-test-designer", "representative_test_data": "data-author"}

